<title>UK: Nynex, Telewest break off bid talk - FT.</title>
<headline>Nynex, Telewest break off bid talk - FT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's two largest cable communications groups Nynex CableComms and Telewest Plc have broken off merger talks after more than a year of on-off negotiations, the Financial Times reported.</p>
<p>The FT said the deal would have created a dominant UK cable company, more able to deal with British Sky Broadcasting, Britain's main cable TV suplier.</p>
<p>Nynex is controlled by NYNEX Corp which is in the process of merging with Bell Atlantic. The FT said Nynex is expected to exit the UK cable market &quot;when the right deal comes along.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717.</p>
</text>
